During the 1976–77 Scottish football season, [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] competed in the [[Scottish Premier Division]].

Celtic won a domestic double as they won both the League by a 9-point margin and the Scottish Cup, defeating [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]] 1-0 in the Final. They narrowly missed on what would have been their third domestic treble as they lost the League Cup Final 1-2 to [[Aberdeen F.C.|Aberdeen]].

Celtic were eliminated from the [[UEFA Cup]] in the first round by [[Wisła Kraków|Wisla Krakow]], 2-4 on aggregate.

